hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"271","We are Bundar, we are Yahya bin Saeed, Ibn Abi Adi, Muhammad bin Jafar, Sahl bin Yusuf, and Abd al-Wahhab bin Abd al-Majid. Al-Thaqafi, they said: Awf told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’ Al-Atardi, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. One night, we traveled until dawn came before dawn, and we had that event. There is no event more beautiful for a traveler than this. The only thing that woke us up was the heat of the sun, so he mentioned some of the hadith and said: Then he called for prayer, and he led some people in prayer, then he left his prayer, and suddenly there was a man secluding himself. He did not pray with the people, so he said to him: “What prevented you, O so-and-so, from praying with the people?” He said: O Messenger of God, I have been afflicted with impurity and there is no water, so he said: “You should go to the desert land, for it is sufficient for you.” Then he walked and the people complained to him, so he called so-and-so. Abu Raja had named it, but Awf forgot it. He called Ali bin Abi Talib and said to them: “Go and seek water for us.” So they set out and received it. A woman was between two tents or two stalls on a camel. He mentioned the hadith and said: Then it was called to the people to water and draw, and whoever wished was watered and drawn. Whoever he wanted, he said: The end of that was that he gave the one who had been afflicted with impurity a vessel of water, and said: “Go, and I will pour it on you.” Abu Bakr said: This report also indicates that if the person performing tayammum prays with tayammum, then he finds water and performs ablution if he is in a state of ritual impurity, or If he has performed ablution, he is not obliged to repeat what he prayed by performing tayammum, since the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not command the person praying to perform tayammum, because He ordered him to perform ablution by repeating what he had prayed by performing tayammum. The report also indicates that the one who has performed ritual ablution due to ritual impurity is not obliged to perform ablution before performing ritual ablution. Spilling water on the body other than the parts of ablution, as the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he commanded the one in a state of ritual impurity to pour water on himself, and he did not He commanded him to begin with ablution and wash the parts for ablution, then pour water over the entire body. He was in his command for as long as he had done. It is correct that if a person in a state of impurity urinates on himself, he is fulfilling his obligation of ghusl, and this is what indicates that the one who is performing ghusl has begun. By performing ablution, then pouring water over the entire body, it is optional and recommended, not obligatory and obligatory."
